{
  "q1_accurate": [
    {"tool": "sense_blast", "query": "nomad.Server", "note": "retained_via_interfaces list directly produced 18 of the narrowed-interface holders I cited (deploymentwatcher, drainer, volumewatcher, periodic, auth.Encrypter, config.RPCHandler, allocrunner RPCer, allocwatcher RPCer, widmgr, HTTPServer, scheduler Planner, FSMHelper); affected_via_composition produced the direct *Server holders by struct"},
    {"tool": "sense_search", "query": "Server struct definition nomad server object", "note": "first hit nomad.Server at nomad/server.go:116 — the exact struct I audited"},
    {"tool": "sense_search", "query": "rpcHandler struct definition", "note": "located nomad.rpcHandler at nomad/rpc.go:47 and newRpcHandler at rpc.go:73"},
    {"tool": "sense_search", "query": "config.RPCHandler", "note": "located client/config/config.go:83 interface and the carrier config.go:161"}
  ],
  "q1_wrong": [
    {"tool": "sense_blast", "query": "nomad.Server", "note": "listed stream.EventBroker.Subscribe/handleACLUpdates as direct_callers 'calls Server' — these are call-site args, not retained fields; I had to read event_broker.go:29 to confirm EventBroker holds no server field and exclude it"},
    {"tool": "sense_blast", "query": "nomad.Server", "note": "retained_via_interfaces listed client/config/config.go:161 RPCHandler as a production holder with chain agent.Agent > nomad.Server, but production code never assigns conf.RPCHandler (only tests do); blast's 'chain' is a declared containment path, not a runtime-wired one — I had to grep the whole repo to confirm it is production-nil"},
    {"tool": "sense_blast", "query": "nomad.Server", "note": "missed deploymentWatcherRaftShim as a retainer entirely — it holds Server only via a function value (apply raftApplyFn, a closure over s.raftApply), which the index caveat explicitly flags as a gap; I found it only by reading deployment_watcher_shims.go and server.go:1160"}
  ],
  "q2_fallbacks": [
    {"tool": "sense_blast", "query": "nomad.Server", "fallback": "read", "missing": "exact field line numbers — blast gives struct line ranges (e.g. acl_endpoint.go:65-79) but not the precise field line; I read each endpoint file to get the srv *Server line (e.g. acl_endpoint.go:66)"},
    {"tool": "sense_blast", "query": "nomad.Server", "fallback": "grep", "missing": "all srv *Server field lines at once — I ran `rg -n '^\\tsrv \\*Server'` over nomad/*.go to enumerate every direct holder in one shot rather than re-reading each file"},
    {"tool": "sense_blast", "query": "nomad.Server", "fallback": "grep", "missing": "whether config.Config.RPCHandler is actually assigned in production — blast's chain asserted carrier agent.Agent > nomad.Server but gave no assignment site; I grepped RPCHandler across the repo to find it is test-only"},
    {"tool": "sense_blast", "query": "nomad.Server", "fallback": "read", "missing": "the deployment watcher shim function-value retention (index_caveat flagged fn-value passing as a gap); I read deployment_watcher_shims.go:15 and server.go:1160 to recover it"},
    {"tool": "sense_blast", "query": "nomad.Server", "fallback": "read", "missing": "EventBroker is a non-retainer — blast listed its methods as 'calls Server' callers; I read event_broker.go:29-45 to confirm no server field and exclude it"},
    {"tool": "sense_blast", "query": "nomad.Server", "fallback": "grep", "missing": "FSMHelper usage sites — blast listed it as retained_via_interfaces with chain nomad.nomadFSM > nomad.Encrypter > nomad.Server but did not say whether the live server uses it; I grepped raftutil. across nomad/ and command/ to confirm it is offline-CLI-only"}
  ],
  "q3_hints": [
    {"tool": "sense_blast", "query_before": "nomad.Server", "query_after": "(switched to grep for RPCHandler assignments)", "hint": "retained_note: 'as indexed... Unverified, and the only unverified part: which satisfier the field holds at runtime' — this disclaimer pushed me to verify config.RPCHandler was actually wired in production rather than trust the chain"},
    {"tool": "sense_blast", "query_before": "nomad.Server", "query_after": "(read deployment_watcher_shims.go + grepped raftApplyFn)", "hint": "index_caveat: 'Static graph may miss... function-value passing (handlers stored as fields)' — this explicitly told me the blast could miss the raftApplyFn closure, so I went looking for it manually"}
  ],
  "q4_value": "The retained_via_interfaces list on the nomad.Server blast — it surfaced the 23 narrowed-interface holders (deploymentwatcher, drainer, volumewatcher, periodic, auth.Encrypter, allocrunner/allocwatcher/widmgr RPCer, HTTPServer, scheduler Planner chains) that have NO compile-time tie to *Server and that grep for '*Server' would have completely missed; this is the core of the audit and the highest-risk dead-handle set.",
  "q5_improve": "On retained_via_interfaces, distinguish runtime-wired chains from merely-declared containment paths — the config.Config.RPCHandler row asserted chain 'agent.Agent > nomad.Server' but in production that field is nil; flagging which chains have an actual assignment site (vs. a possible interface-satisfaction edge) would have saved a full-repo grep to separate live holders from dormant fields.",
  "score": 8,
  "score_rationale": "Blast's retained_via_interfaces gave me the narrowed-interface holders — the exact high-risk set grep could not have produced — and the index_caveat hint correctly drove me to the fn-value gap (Q1/Q3), but I still needed ~6 read/grep fallbacks to recover exact field lines, verify which chains are runtime-wired, exclude EventBroker, and find the raftApplyFn shim (Q2), so it sits at the top of the 7-8 band rather than 9."
}
